<%# decor/app/views/storage_locations/delete_confirm.html.erb - version 1.0 %>
<%# Session B (Storage Locations feature). %>
<%#
INTERIM — NOT the final design. See storage_locations_controller.rb v1.0's
class-level comment for the full explanation: storage_location.rb v1.0's own
header comment calls for this view to "warn with counts" of affected
computers/components/software_items before destroy, but those associations
don't exist yet (deferred to Session C). Since nothing can reference a
StorageLocation until Session C ships, there is nothing real to count —
this shows a plain, honest confirmation instead of guessing at Session C's
eventual association/method names.

Session C MUST replace this file's body with a real counts warning (e.g.
"N computers, N components, and N software items currently use this
location and will be set to no location") once
has_many :computers/:components/:software_items exist on StorageLocation.

Delete link pattern matches admin/site_texts/delete_confirm.html.erb v1.1's
precedent: data: { turbo_method: :delete, turbo_confirm: ... } on a plain
link, NOT wrapped in any data-turbo="false" ancestor (see RAILS_SPECIFICS.md
"data-turbo='false' — NEVER wrap Turbo-method links inside it" — this file
has no such wrapper at all, so that trap doesn't apply here).
%>

<div class="max-w-lg mx-auto">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Delete Storage Location</h1>

  <div class="mb-6 p-3 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded text-sm text-amber-800">
    Delete "<strong><%= @storage_location.name %></strong>"? This cannot be undone.
  </div>

  <div class="flex gap-3 items-center">
    <%= link_to "Delete",
          storage_location_path(@storage_location),
          data: { turbo_method: :delete,
                  turbo_confirm: "Delete this storage location? This cannot be undone." },
          class: "#{button_classes(style: :primary)} bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-700" %>
    <%= link_to "Cancel", storage_locations_path, class: button_classes(style: :secondary) %>
  </div>
</div>
